# No mouse cursor from a pad's touchpad (the round-4 pad plan, D4). A DualShock 4 / DualSense also shows its touchpad
# and its motion sensors as input devices; Weston (libinput 1.4.1 on the console) took the touchpad as a pointer and
# drew a cursor over every App. That libinput does not know LIBINPUT_IGNORE_DEVICE and does not care that ID_INPUT_*
# were cleared (the kernel payload's 99-autobleem-no-pointer.rules does both) - but it does skip a device whose
# ID_SEAT is not its own seat (seat0). So these nodes get a seat nobody runs. SDL and abpadd do not read ID_SEAT.
# rc/pad_seat.sh installs this file into /run/udev/rules.d at boot (tmpfs - nothing on the console's own storage) for a
# kernel payload that does not carry the same line yet. A real USB mouse is left alone.
ACTION!="remove", SUBSYSTEM=="input", KERNEL=="event*", ATTRS{name}=="*Wireless Controller Touchpad|*DualSense*Touchpad|*DualShock*Touchpad|*Wireless Controller Motion Sensors|*DualSense*Motion Sensors|*DualShock*Motion Sensors", ENV{ID_SEAT}="seat-autobleem-none"
